h": 352905740, "N": 8857, "br": 31.354, "dbr": -1.617, "dh": -3.64}], "statements": {"n": 32, "from": "2019-10-22", "last": [{"d": "2026-10-22", "n": 2.82, "z": 0.51, "rz": 0.39, "earn": true, "q": "Our strong third quarter performance underscores Lockheed Martin’s continuing leadership in the development and delivery of advanced and reliable defense technology solutions. Every day, our research, engineering and production teams are putting highly effective and scalable capabilities in the field. We strive to impr…", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828026066780/ex991q32026.htm"}, {"d": "2026-07-23", "n": 2.97, "z": 0.73, "rz": 0.04, "earn": true, "q": "We delivered strong second‑quarter performance, with over $20 billion in sales – a year‑over‑year increase of 11% – free cash flow of $2.9 billion, and $65 billion of new orders, which takes our backlog to a record $230 billion. This continued performance reflects more than just increased customer demand – it is eviden…", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828026049277/ex991q22026.htm"}, {"d": "2026-04-23", "n": 1.45, "z": -0.63, "rz": 0.54, "earn": true, "q": "Lockheed Martin’s superior capabilities in delivering advanced defense technology and systems and in space exploration have been proven again and again in 2026. Our Orion spacecraft safely carried the crew farther from Earth than ever before during NASA’s historic Artemis II mission, concluding with a precisely execute…", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828026026683/ex991q12026.htm"}, {"d": "2026-01-29", "n": 1.02, "z": -1.11, "rz": -0.37, "earn": true, "q": "With a record $194 billion backlog, 6% year-over-year sales growth, and free cash flow generation above our prior expectation, 2025 marked a year of unprecedented demand for Lockheed Martin capabilities. This escalating demand for our signature programs and systems has been driven by combat-proven performance over rece…", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet. “To ensure we continue delivering overwhelming capability at speed and scale, ", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828026003970/ex991q42025.htm"}, {"d": "2025-10-21", "n": 2.21, "z": 0.04, "rz": 0.45, "earn": true, "q": "Based on the effectiveness and reliability of our products and systems, strong demand from Lockheed Martin’s customers—both in the United States and among our allies—continues. As a result of this unprecedented demand, we are increasing production capacity significantly across a wide range of our lines of business,", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President, and CEO Jim Taiclet. “Our record $179 billion backlog—more than two and a half years of sales—unde", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828025045582/ex991q32025.htm"}, {"d": "2025-07-22", "n": 0.41, "z": -1.37, "rz": -4.3, "earn": true, "q": "Over the course of the past few months, Lockheed Martin systems and platforms once again proved highly effective in combat operations and in deterring further aggression. Our F-35s, F-22s, PAC-3, THAAD, Aegis and many others, crewed by the soldiers, aircrews, sailors, marines and guardians of the U.S. and its Allies, a…", "a": "said Lockheed Martin Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet. “Based in part on this record of performance as well as the promise of several", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000162828025035502/ex991q22025.htm"}], "now": {"d": "2026-10-22", "z": 0.51, "mood": "usual"}, "say_do": {"mood": "usual", "acts": "sell", "clash": false, "agree": false}}, "score": {"value": 52, "verdict": {"it": "Nessuna convinzione chiara", "en": "No clear conviction"}, "confidence": "Media", "covered_pct": 80